-silence-vultures-city.md","Era of Silence — Vulture's City (PDF)",{"type":188,"value":224,"toc":230},[225],[191,226,227],{},[194,228,197],{"href":229},"/downloads/stories/Era-of-Silence_-Vultures-City.pdf",{"title":199,"searchDepth":200,"depth":200,"links":231},[],"2025-03-25T00:00:00.000Z","Downloadable PDF edition of Vulture's City.",{"slug":235},"era-of-silence-vultures-city","/resources/era-of-silence-vultures-city",{"title":222,"description":233},"resources/era-of-silence-vultures-city",[20,240,216,217],"Vulture's City","3OOX8PUZgY8KRCvzM9W-IN2WJYz7Ei1NHenJrT3dagc",{"id":243,"title":244,"body":245,"category":202,"date":425,"description":426,"download":427,"downloadUrl":202,"extension":205,"external":206,"file":202,"fileSize":202,"game":207,"image":202,"meta":428,"navigation":210,"pageCount":202,"path":430,"published":210,"seo":431,"stem":432,"tags":433,"type":436,"updatedAt":202,"url":202,"__hash__":437},"resources/resources/era-of-silence-quick-reference.md","Era of Silence - Quick Reference Guide",{"type":188,"value":246,"toc":411},[247,251,256,262,266,271,287,291,312,316,337,341,361,365,369,372,383,387,398,401],[248,249,244],"h1",{"id":250},"era-of-silence-quick-reference-guide",[252,253,255],"h2",{"id":254},"game-overview","Game Overview",[191,257,258,261],{},[259,260,20],"em",{}," is a strategic card game for 2-4 players. In a world where words can kill, players must carefully manage when to speak and when to remain silent.",[252,263,265],{"id":264},"core-mechanics","Core Mechanics",[267,268,270],"h3",{"id":269},"the-silence-meter","The Silence Meter",[272,273,274,278,281,284],"ul",{},[275,276,277],"li",{},"Starts at 0",[275,279,280],{},"Increases when players speak (play cards)",[275,282,283],{},"When it reaches 10, triggers the Silence Cascade",[275,285,286],{},"Players can spend actions to reduce the meter",[267,288,290],{"id":289},"card-types","Card Types",[272,292,293,300,306],{},[275,294,295,299],{},[296,297,298],"strong",{},"Action Cards",": Perform game effects but increase the Silence Meter",[275,301,302,305],{},[296,303,304],{},"Silence Cards",": Reduce the Silence Meter or protect against cascades",[275,307,308,311],{},[296,309,310],{},"Event Cards",": Trigger special game effects",[267,313,315],{"id":314},"player-actions","Player Actions",[317,318,319,325,331],"ol",{},[275,320,321,324],{},[296,322,323],{},"Play Card",": Choose a card from hand to play",[275,326,327,330],{},[296,328,329],{},"Pass",": Skip your turn (safe but limited)",[275,332,333,336],{},[296,334,335],{},"Communicate",": Use hand signals to coordinate with allies",[252,338,340],{"id":339},"win-conditions","Win Conditions",[272,342,343,349,355],{},[275,344,345,348],{},[296,346,347],{},"Elimination",": Last player standing when others are silenced",[275,350,351,354],{},[296,352,353],{},"Objective",": Complete your secret objective before others",[275,356,357,360],{},[296,358,359],{},"Alliance",": Work with others to achieve mutual goals",[252,362,364],{"id":363},"advanced-rules","Advanced Rules",[267,366,368],{"id":367},"cascades","Cascades",[191,370,371],{},"When the Silence Meter reaches 10:",[272,373,374,377,380],{},[275,375,376],{},"All players discard cards",[275,378,379],{},"Special cascade effects trigger",[275,381,382],{},"Meter resets to 5",[267,384,386],{"id":385},"communication-limits","Communication Limits",[272,388,389,392,395],{},[275,390,391],{},"No verbal communication during play",[275,393,394],{},"Hand signals allowed",[275,396,397],{},"Written notes permitted but risky",[191,399,400],{},"Download the full rulebook for complete mechanics and strategy guides.",[191,402,403,407,408],{},[194,404,406],{"href":405},"/downloads/reference/era-of-silence-rulebook.pdf","Download Full Rulebook"," | ",[194,409,410],{"href":21},"Back to Game",{"title":199,"searchDepth":200,"depth":200,"links":412},[413,414,420,421],{"id":254,"depth":200,"text":255},{"id":264,"depth":200,"text":265,"children":415},[416,418,419],{"id":269,"depth":417,"text":270},3,{"id":289,"depth":417,"text":290},{"id":314,"depth":417,"text":315},{"id":339,"depth":200,"text":340},{"id":363,"depth":200,"text":364,"children":422},[423,424],{"id":367,"depth":417,"text":368},{"id":385,"depth":417,"text":386},"2024-09-20T00:00:00.000Z","Essential rules and mechanics for Era of Silence in a convenient reference format.","/downloads/reference/era-of-silence-quick-reference.pdf",{"slug":429},"era-of-silence-quick-reference","/resources/era-of-silence-quick-reference",{"title":244,"description":426},"resources/era-of-silence-quick-reference",[20,434,435],"Rules","Quick Reference","quick-reference","ifSZc4sZe4Wwfw12mFRPkesg6fHwVSizRPw2NiHQRFk",{"id":439,"title":440,"body":441,"category":202,"date":691,"description":692,"download":202,"downloadUrl":202,"extension":205,"external":206,"file":202,"fileSize":202,"game":202,"image":693,"meta":694,"navigation":210,"pageCount":202,"path":695,"published":210,"seo":696,"stem":697,"tags":698,"type":703,"updatedAt":202,"url":619,"__hash__":704},"resources/resources/left-wing-game-design-reading-list.md","Left-Wing Game Design Reading List",{"type":188,"value":442,"toc":677},[443,446,450,453,457,460,474,478,482,485,490,510,514,517,522,542,546,549,553,573,577,580,584,604,608,611,615,624,631,635,643,654,658],[248,444,440],{"id":445},"left-wing-game-design-reading-list",[252,447,449],{"id":448},"overview","Overview",[191,451,452],{},"A living document of books, essays, games, and other resources for designers who want to make games about solidarity, systemic change, and collective power—without being preachy or reductive.",[252,454,456],{"id":455},"what-youll-find","What You'll Find",[191,458,459],{},"This isn't just theory—it's theory in conversation with practical game design. Each entry includes:",[272,461,462,465,468,471],{},[275,463,464],{},"Why it matters for game design",[275,466,467],{},"Key concepts that translate to mechanics",[275,469,470],{},"Games that demonstrate these ideas",[275,472,473],{},"Questions to ask about your own work",[252,475,477],{"id":476},"major-sections","Major Sections",[267,479,481],{"id":480},"labor-work","Labor & Work",[191,483,484],{},"From union organizing to emotional labor, how do we represent work in games beyond resource extraction?",[191,486,487],{},[296,488,489],{},"Featured texts:",[272,491,492,498,504],{},[275,493,494,495],{},"Kathi Weeks, ",[259,496,497],{},"The Problem with Work",[275,499,500,501],{},"David Graeber, ",[259,502,503],{},"Bullshit Jobs",[275,505,506,507],{},"Kim Stanley Robinson, ",[259,508,509],{},"The Ministry for the Future",[267,511,513],{"id":512},"collective-action","Collective Action",[191,515,516],{},"What does solidarity look like as a game mechanic? How do we design cooperation that isn't just \"players versus environment\"?",[191,518,519],{},[296,520,521],{},"Featured games:",[272,523,524,530,536],{},[275,525,526,529],{},[259,527,528],{},"Bloc by Bloc"," (board game)",[275,531,532,535],{},[259,533,534],{},"Tonight We Riot"," (video game)",[275,537,538,541],{},[259,539,540],{},"Good Society"," (TTRPG)",[267,543,545],{"id":544},"systems-thinking","Systems Thinking",[191,547,548],{},"Understanding capitalism as a system, not a collection of evil individuals. How do we model structural problems?",[191,550,551],{},[296,552,489],{},[272,554,555,561,567],{},[275,556,557,558],{},"Ursula K. Le Guin, ",[259,559,560],{},"The Dispossessed",[275,562,563,564],{},"Octavia Butler, ",[259,565,566],{},"Parable of the Sower",[275,568,569,570],{},"Rebecca Solnit, ",[259,571,572],{},"A Paradise Built in Hell",[267,574,576],{"id":575},"alternatives-futures","Alternatives & Futures",[191,578,579],{},"Imagining post-capitalist worlds without falling into naive utopianism.",[191,581,582],{},[296,583,521],{},[272,585,586,592,598],{},[275,587,588,591],{},[259,589,590],{},"Dialect"," (TTRPG about language and community)",[275,593,594,597],{},[259,595,596],{},"The Quiet Year"," (map-drawing game)",[275,599,600,603],{},[259,601,602],{},"Dream Askew/Dream Apart"," (queer community survival)",[267,605,607],{"id":606},"mechanics-of-liberation","Mechanics of Liberation",[191,609,610],{},"Specific game mechanics that embody leftist principles: shared resources, collective decision-making, mutual aid, etc.",[252,612,614],{"id":613},"access-the-full-list","Access the Full List",[191,616,617,623],{},[194,618,622],{"href":619,"rel":620},"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1234567890abcdef",[621],"nofollow","View on Google Docs"," (Comment access enabled)",[191,625,626,627,630],{},"This is a ",[296,628,629],{},"living document",". We add resources regularly and welcome suggestions from the community.",[252,632,634],{"id":633},"contribute","Contribute",[191,636,637,638,642],{},"Know a resource that should be on this list? Email us at ",[194,639,641],{"href":640},"mailto:contact@shrikepublishing.com","contact@shrikepublishing.com"," with:",[272,644,645,648,651],{},[275,646,647],{},"Resource name and creator",[275,649,650],{},"Brief description (2-3 sentences)",[275,652,653],{},"Why it's useful for game designers",[252,655,657],{"id":656},"related","Related",[272,659,660,666,672],{},[275,661,662],{},[194,663,665],{"href":664},"/resources/solarpunk-worldbuilding-toolkit","Solarpunk Worldbuilding Toolkit",[275,667,668,669,671],{},"Our ",[194,670,44],{"href":45}," for game design essays",[275,673,674,676],{},[194,675,12],{"href":17}," we've published",{"title":199,"searchDepth":200,"depth":200,"links":678},[679,680,681,688,689,690],{"id":448,"depth":200,"text":449},{"id":455,"depth":200,"text":456},{"id":476,"depth":200,"text":477,"children":682},[683,684,685,686,687],{"id":480,"depth":417,"text":481},{"id":512,"depth":417,"text":513},{"id":544,"depth":417,"text":545},{"id":575,"depth":417,"text":576},{"id":606,"depth":417,"text":607},{"id":613,"depth":200,"text":614},{"id":633,"depth":200,"text":634},{"id":656,"depth":200,"text":657},"2024-08-15T00:00:00.000Z","Curated resources for designing games that engage with class, labor, collective action, and systemic change. Theory meets mechanics.","/images/resources/reading-list-placeholder.jpg",{"slug":445},"/resources/left-wing-game-design-reading-list",{"title":440,"description":692},"resources/left-wing-game-design-reading-list",[699,700,701,702],"game-design","political-theory","labor","resource-list","link","6-prQKDgJntnvhgiWac-AC8x7HCLQXWTUgfCLv0YhTY",{"id":706,"title":707,"body":708,"category":202,"date":932,"description":933,"download":202,"downloadUrl":202,"extension":205,"external":206,"file":202,"fileSize":202,"game":202,"image":934,"meta":935,"navigation":210,"pageCount":202,"path":937,"published":210,"seo":938,"stem":939,"tags":940,"type":941,"updatedAt":202,"url":874,"__hash__":945},"resources/resources/sci-fi-name-generator.md","Science Fantasy Name Generator",{"type":188,"value":709,"toc":917},[710,713,715,718,722,726,740,744,758,762,776,780,794,798,801,827,831,848,852,866,870,877,882,886,889,898,902],[248,711,707],{"id":712},"science-fantasy-name-generator",[252,714,449],{"id":448},[191,716,717],{},"Generate names for your science fantasy worlds that sound plausible, are pronounceable, and don't feel like keyboard-mashing. Perfect for NPCs, planets, starships, and that corporation that definitely isn't evil (but totally is).",[252,719,721],{"id":720},"features","Features",[267,723,725],{"id":724},"character-names","Character Names",[272,727,728,731,734,737],{},[275,729,730],{},"Human names with cultural mixing (because the future is syncretic)",[275,732,733],{},"Alien names with consistent phonetic patterns",[275,735,736],{},"Nicknames and callsigns",[275,738,739],{},"Full name + title generators",[267,741,743],{"id":742},"place-names","Place Names",[272,745,746,749,752,755],{},[275,747,748],{},"Planets and moons",[275,750,751],{},"Space stations and habitats",[275,753,754],{},"Cities and settlements",[275,756,757],{},"Geographic features",[267,759,761],{"id":760},"ship-names","Ship Names",[272,763,764,767,770,773],{},[275,765,766],{},"Corporate vessels (sterile and bureaucratic)",[275,768,769],{},"Military ships (dramatic and intimidating)",[275,771,772],{},"Independent traders (quirky and personal)",[275,774,775],{},"Generation ships (hopeful and ominous)",[267,777,779],{"id":778},"organization-names","Organization Names",[272,781,782,785,788,791],{},[275,783,784],{},"Corporations (evil and/or banal)",[275,786,787],{},"Resistance movements (aspirational)",[275,789,790],{},"Guilds and unions",[275,792,793],{},"Religious/philosophical orders",[252,795,797],{"id":796},"how-it-works","How It Works",[191,799,800],{},"Unlike AI generators that produce unpronounceable garbage, this tool uses:",[272,802,803,809,815,821],{},[275,804,805,808],{},[296,806,807],{},"Phonetic pattern libraries"," from real languages",[275,810,811,814],{},[296,812,813],{},"Customizable syllable structures"," for consistency",[275,816,817,820],{},[296,818,819],{},"Cultural mixing algorithms"," for realistic diaspora naming",[275,822,823,826],{},[296,824,825],{},"Semantic meaning options"," (optional - for when you want names to mean something)",[252,828,830],{"id":829},"settings-customization","Settings & Customization",[272,832,833,836,839,842,845],{},[275,834,835],{},"Adjust syllable count (2-5)",[275,837,838],{},"Choose phonetic complexity (simple to complex)",[275,840,841],{},"Set cultural influences (East Asian, Latinate, Arabic, Synthetic, etc.)",[275,843,844],{},"Generate in batches (10-50 at once)",[275,846,847],{},"Export to text or JSON",[252,849,851],{"id":850},"use-cases","Use Cases",[272,853,854,857,860,863],{},[275,855,856],{},"\"I need 20 NPC names for tonight's game session\"",[275,858,859],{},"\"What should I name this definitely-not-Weyland-Yutani megacorp?\"",[275,861,862],{},"\"My generation ship needs a name that sounds both hopeful and ominous\"",[275,864,865],{},"\"I'm worldbuilding and need consistent place names for an entire solar system\"",[252,867,869],{"id":868},"try-it-now","Try It Now",[191,871,872],{},[194,873,876],{"href":874,"rel":875},"https://shrikepublishing.com/tools/name-generator",[621],"Launch Name Generator",[191,878,879],{},[296,880,881],{},"100% free, no account required, no data collection.",[252,883,885],{"id":884},"technical-notes","Technical Notes",[191,887,888],{},"Built with vanilla JavaScript because sometimes simplicity is a virtue. Works offline once loaded (progressive web app).",[191,890,891,892,897],{},"Source code available on ",[194,893,896],{"href":894,"rel":895},"https://github.com/shrikepublishing/name-generator",[621],"GitHub"," under MIT license.",[252,899,901],{"id":900},"related-resources","Related Resources",[272,903,904,908,912],{},[275,905,906],{},[194,907,665],{"href":664},[275,909,910],{},[194,911,440],{"href":695},[275,913,668,914,916],{},[194,915,36],{"href":37}," for naming inspiration",{"title":199,"searchDepth":200,"depth":200,"links":918},[919,920,926,927,928,929,930,931],{"id":448,"depth":200,"text":449},{"id":720,"depth":200,"text":721,"children":921},[922,923,924,925],{"id":724,"depth":417,"text":725},{"id":742,"depth":417,"text":743},{"id":760,"depth":417,"text":761},{"id":778,"depth":417,"text":779},{"id":796,"depth":200,"text":797},{"id":829,"depth":200,"text":830},{"id":850,"depth":200,"text":851},{"id":868,"depth":200,"text":869},{"id":884,"depth":200,"text":885},{"id":900,"depth":200,"text":901},"2024-07-10T00:00:00.000Z","Browser-based tool for generating character, place, and ship names that sound science-y without being unpronounceable. No AI slop, just good phonetics.","/images/resources/name-generator-placeholder.jpg",{"slug":936},"sci-fi-name-generator","/resources/sci-fi-name-generator",{"title":707,"description":933},"resources/sci-fi-name-generator",[941,942,943,944],"tool","worldbuilding","character-creation","web-app","iPX8iwVLYo121Z1-YV4j_4-jNZp04PCieitPXLwsQN8",{"id":947,"title":948,"body":949,"category":202,"date":958,"description":959,"download":955,